                  { code: '13',
                    prompt: "Using the rules of Boolean algebra, simplify the following Boolean expression.\n\n    NOT(A · B + Ā · C + B · C + B̄ · A)\n\n(In the question paper a single overbar covers the whole expression.)\n\nYou must show your working.", marks: 4 }
