                  'Enforcing laws: Electronic evidence may be harder to gather than physical evidence // can be harder to identify culprits online (A. an example of a system that makes it harder to identify the culprit, e.g. use of proxies, encryption, VPN, computers owned by innocent individuals but controlled by a criminal, use of peer-to-peer systems; NE. harder to catch criminals)',
                  'Enforcing laws: Resources required to enforce legislation may not be available // large volume of users/data makes it difficult/impossible to effectively monitor'
