                  'General purpose registers: Store values that instructions can/will use as operands / will be carried out on // store the results of executing instructions // store the results of calculations (A. store intermediate results during calculations; A. store values being processed; TO. store instructions)',
                  'General purpose registers: The programmer determines the (exact) role of each register (when writing a program) (NE. store values inside the processor)',
                  'Status register: Stores information about the result of the last (arithmetic/logical) instruction',
                  'Status register: Contents are used to affect the behaviour of the next instruction / subsequent instructions // to control conditional branch instructions',
