              '09.3': { type: 'points', points: ['1 mark for final answer: A', 'Working (up to 3 marks): 1 mark per successful application of De Morgan\'s Law (and any associated cancellation of NOTs) that produces a simpler expression – award 2 marks if De Morgan\'s Law is applied twice simultaneously', 'Working: 1 mark per application of an identity other than cancelling NOTs that produces a simpler expression', 'Working: 1 mark per successful expansion of brackets / factorising (multiple marks can be awarded for using the same technique more than once)'], guidance: '4 marks (1 answer + max 3 working). All marks AO2. Award marks for working until an incorrect step has been made. Ignore missing steps as long as the jumps between steps are logically correct. If simplifying different parts simultaneously and an error is made, award marks for the correctly simplified part(s) then stop marking. A simpler expression is logically equivalent but uses fewer logical operators. Max 2 for working if there is no successful application of De Morgan. Max 3 overall if any incorrect working. Example solution: A·B̄ + B·NOT(Ā + B̄·C) → A·B̄ + B·A·NOT(B̄·C) [De Morgan] → A·(B̄ + B·NOT(B̄·C)) [factorising] → A·(B̄ + B·(B + C̄)) [De Morgan] → A·(B̄ + B·B + B·C̄) [expand] → A·(B̄ + B + B·C̄) [X·X = X] → A·(1 + B·C̄) [X + X̄ = 1] → A·1 [X + 1 = 1] → A [X·1 = X]. Alternative: A·B̄ + A·B·(B + C̄) → A·B̄ + A·B + A·B·C̄ → A·(B̄ + B) + A·B·C̄ → A + A·B·C̄ → A [X + X·Y = X].' },
