                  'AO2 — Application': 'Moral: individuals may not know that their images are being used to train the AI; individuals are entitled to privacy and may not want their photograph used — they may see it as an invasion of privacy; the AI searches the internet randomly so it needs to ensure it uses a complete range of diverse photographs (people from different cultures, diversity of scenes) to represent reality and ensure fairness. Legal: photographs must be accessed legally without criminal activity so the Computer Misuse Act is not breached; organisations must keep personal data (including photos) safe under the Data Protection Act, so must ensure these cannot be accessed by the AI; some images are protected by the Copyright, Designs and Patents Act (people\'s intellectual property) and cannot be accessed without permission from the author.',
