                  'AO1 — Knowledge': 'OOP allows any number of elements... a new object is created each time... do not need to declare the number of elements. An array needs to know the number of elements. OOP can be reused in other programs for other lists without having to make significant changes; an array would need more changes for other programs, such as the size of the array. An array needs a way to indicate which elements have been used and which are empty.',
