              '4(b)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['Succession (has occurred)', 'Samphire is a {pioneer (species) / coloniser} (allow samphire is the only species that can live close to water / only samphire has adaptations to live by water)', 'Samphire roots bind the silt / stabilise soil / stabilise substrate', 'More {organic matter / humus} (in silt) due to {death / decomposition} (of plants) / more {nutrients / minerals / named nutrients} in soil (for other plant species) (allow increased soil depth due to decomposition; allow decay)', 'Competition from {sea lavender / scurvy grass} results in less samphire (allow plants have different niches; allow competition between scurvy grass and sea lavender)', 'Abiotic factors change further in from the sea / more sheltered further from sea (allow named factors e.g. less wind / less salt / less exposed / less often flooded)'], guidance: '4 marks. Any four of the six points.' },
