              '02.4': { type: 'points', points: ['Yield would increase', 'Equilibrium opposes temperature increase', 'Moves in the endothermic direction'], guidance: '3 marks (AO2 ×3). Shifts /moves to reduce temperature Ignore favours' },
              '02.5': { type: 'points', points: ['Causes ozone depletion/decomposition/damage', 'Pentane does not have C-Cl bonds'], guidance: '2 marks (AO1 ×2). Accept hole in the ozone layer Accept does not produce Cl radicals Accept does not contain chlorine' },
              '03.1': { type: 'points', points: ['M1 Electrophilic addition', 'M2: must show an arrow from = of C=C towards the H atom of the H–O bond or HO that is part of H–O–S–… on a compound with molecular formula H₂SO₄ (M2 could have arrow to H⁺ in which case M3 would be for an independent H–O bond break on a compound with formula H₂SO₄)', 'M3: must use an arrow to show the breaking of the H–O bond', 'M4: is for the correct carbocation structure, (CH₃)₂C⁺CH₂CH₃ [drawn]', 'M5: must show an arrow from a lone pair of electrons on the correct oxygen of the negatively charged ion towards the positively charged carbon atom'], guidance: '5 marks (AO1 ×1; AO2 ×4). NB Allow fully displayed or other structural formulae if H₂O used as electrophile – max 4 ONLY M3 ignore partial charges unless wrong NOT M4 if primary carbocation shown. M5 NOT HSO₄ credit as shown or as :OSO₃H – in which case negative charge can be shown anywhere ECF from H₂SO₃ in M2 IGNORE subsequent use of water to hydrolyse hydrogensulfate NB: The arrows are double-headed. [Mechanism drawn: 2-methylbut-1-ene + H₂SO₄.]' },
              '03.2': { type: 'points', points: ['M1 structure of minor product CH₂(OSO₂OH)CH(CH₃)CH₂CH₃ [drawn]', 'M2 (major) product formed via more stable carbocation OR tertiary carbocation more stable (than primary)', 'M3 Due to electron-releasing character / (positive) inductive effect of three alkyl groups (as opposed to one)'], guidance: '3 marks (AO2 ×3). If tertiary shown here allow as ECF for M1 if primary shown in 03.1 Must be clear refers to intermediate and not product Primary has one e⁻ donating alkyl group' },
              '03.3': { type: 'points', points: ['Skeletal formula of a C₅H₁₀ cycloalkane: cyclopentane, methylcyclobutane, 1,2-dimethylcyclopropane, 1,1-dimethylcyclopropane or ethylcyclopropane [drawn]'], guidance: '1 mark (AO1). ignore structure of 2-methylbut-1-ene' },
              '03.4': { type: 'points', points: ['M1 Addition (polymerisation)', 'M2 repeat unit –CH₂–C(CH₃)(CH₂CH₃)– with trailing bonds [drawn]'], guidance: '2 marks (AO1 ×1; AO2 ×1). Not additional Penalise incorrect attachment of ethyl group Must have trailing bonds Ignore n and brackets Ignore structure of 2-methylbut-1-ene' },
