              '09.2': { type: 'points', points: ['M1 Ratio Y : bromine 1 : 5', 'M2 n Y in 25 cm³ oil = (7.5 x 10⁻⁴)/5 = 1.5 × 10⁻⁴ (if no ratio must state n Y for M2)', 'M3 n Y in 250 cm³ = M2 × 10 = (1.5 × 10⁻³)', 'M4 Mass = M3 × 880 = (1.32 g)', 'M5 Total mass oil needed = M4 × 100/85 = 1.55 g'], guidance: '5 marks (AO2 ×3; AO3 ×2). Alternative calc using supplied answer: n Y in 25 cm³ oil = (6.25 x 10⁻⁴)/5 = 1.25 × 10⁻⁴; n Y in 250 cm³ = 1.25 × 10⁻⁴ × 10 = (1.25 × 10⁻³); Mass = 1.25 × 10⁻³ × 880 = (1.1 g); Total mass oil needed = 1.1 × 100/85 = 1.29 g. If wrong ratio used treat as AE and mark ECF.' },
              '09.3': { type: 'points', points: ['Extra step: Weigh the bottle after oil transfer (and record the mass)', 'Justification: Not all of the oil is transferred Or so that the mass of oil left in the bottle is accounted for Or find the exact mass of oil used'], guidance: '2 marks (AO3 ×2). OR Rinse the bottle with solvent after transfer and add the washings (to the volumetric flask) To ensure all the oil is transferred M2 is dependent on M1' },
