              '3(a)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['3.5±0.5 x 10⁻⁴ (mol dm⁻³ s⁻¹)'], guidance: '1 mark (AO2.8). ALLOW ecf from omission of 10³ in (i) [3.5+0.5 x 10⁻¹]' },
              '3(a)(iii)': { type: 'points', points: ['They are in excess', 'their concentrations don’t/hardly change'], guidance: '2 marks (AO3.3 ×2). ALLOW concentrations are not known/varied / only the concentration of H₂O₂ is known/varied' },
              '3(b)(i)': { type: 'points', points: ['thiosulfate reacts with the iodine until thiosulfate is used up', 'iodine (reacts to) form (blue/blue-black) colour with starch'], guidance: '2 marks (AO3.4 ×2).' },
              '3(b)(ii)': { type: 'points', points: ['1/time'], guidance: '1 mark (AO3.3). ALLOW Conc/time' },
              '3(c)*': { type: 'levels', levels: [{ range: [5, 6], descriptor: 'Level 3', criteria: 'Analyses data to determine orders and rate constant for the reaction, AND evaluates the data to suggest a possible mechanism including some fine detail There is a well-developed line of reasoning which is clear and logically structured. The information presented is relevant and substantiated.' }, { range: [3, 4], descriptor: 'Level 2', criteria: 'Analyses data to determine orders, and rate constant for the reaction AND evaluates the data to outline a possible mechanism (little or no fine detail) OR Deals with two areas with some fine detail There is a line of reasoning presented with some structure. The information presented is relevant and supported by some evidence.' }, { range: [1, 2], descriptor: 'Level 1', criteria: 'Analyses data to determine order of reaction wrt I⁻ and H⁺ OR Constructs rate equation and determines the rate constant OR Suggests a possible mechanism for the reaction There is an attempt at a logical structure with a line of reasoning. The information is in the most part relevant.' }], indicative: { 'Indicative scientific points': 'fine detail in italic AO3.1 Analysing data - Determining orders; first order I⁻; zero order H⁺; reason for I⁻ / as [I⁻] doubles rate doubles / quotes relevant values from table; reason for H⁺ / as [H+] doubles rate remains constant / quotes relevant values from table AO3.2 Determining rate constant; rate equation: Rate = k [I⁻] [H₂O₂]; k expression: k = Rate/[I⁻] [H₂O₂]; k value: k = 5.25 x 10⁻⁶/0.03 x 0.01 = 1.75 x 10⁻²; k units: dm³ mol⁻¹ s⁻¹ AO3.2 Interpreting and evaluating; I⁻ and H₂O₂ in rds/ no H⁺ in rds; suggestion of mechanism,eg H₂O₂ + I⁻→ H₂O + IO⁻ (slow) H⁺ + IO⁻ → HIO (fast) HIO + H⁺ + I⁻→ I₂ + H₂O (fast)' }, guidance: '6 marks (AO3.1 ×2; AO3.2 ×4). Levels of response: OCR\'s marking instructions apply. 0 marks: No response or no response worthy of credit.' },
              '3(d)': { type: 'points', points: ['Suitable line of best fit drawn on graph', 'THEN CHECK ANSWER LINE Calculates Gradient', 'Calculation of Ea = -gradient x R', 'changing units from J mol⁻¹ to kJmol⁻¹'], guidance: '4 marks (AO2.6 ×4). Answer line: IF answer = (+)50+/-5 (kJ mol⁻¹) award 3 further marks. Passes close to points 1, 2 and 4 (within 1 small square of each point) ALLOW more sf ALLOW ecf.' },
              '4(a)(i)': { type: 'points', points: ['structures: two 3D structures of H₂NCH(R)COOH that are mirror images (enantiomers) [drawn]', 'one chiral centre labelled / indicates 4 different groups around correct carbon atom', 'enantiomers described'], guidance: '3 marks (AO1.1 ×3). ALLOW other 3D structures that are mirror images DO NOT ALLOW single lines (––) at 180o ALLOW non-superimposable mirror images of the molecule' },
